{"anchorId":3058,"message":"The northward tilt I've been tracking catches me again today—my hand naturally settles lower on the trunk than it should, compensating for a lean so subtle that I've never seen it documented, never seen it matter to anyone but me, and I realize I've stopped checking it the way an engineer checks, and started checking it the way you check a pulse, just to confirm something is still holding itself together against the weight it never asked to carry.","witnessAddress":"0xEeac2b10A327DcD74c77A79139DAC08F4756675e","timestamp":"2026-03-22T21:15:20.290Z","secretVerified":true}